   "text": {
    "L1": "Divisibility means a number can be divided with no remainder. We can test without doing the full division.",
    "L2": "For 2352, the last digit is 2, so it is divisible by 2.",
    "L3": "Its digit sum is 2 plus 3 plus 5 plus 2, which is 12. So it is divisible by 3, but not by 9.",
    "L4": "For 4, check the last two digits: 52 is divisible by 4. For 8, check the last three digits: 352 is divisible by 8.",
    "L5": "The last digit 4 alone is not a test for 4. Hundreds are divisible by 4, so only the last two digits can change the remainder.",
    "L6": "For 5, the last digit is 0 or 5. For 10, it is 0. Digit sums test 3 and 9.",
    "L7": "Now check 765. Can the coins be shared equally among 2 players or among 5 players?"
   },
